 "diagnosis": "Numerical, not physical: a slow frictional settling drift of the mesh-3 body at dtScale 0.5. It vanishes when dt is halved (5.9e-9 L), when friction is removed (1.7e-14 L), without gravity (exactly 0), with the 1 s settle (1.8e-7 L) and with the stiffer-damped constant-zeta policy (1.6e-8 L); doubling collision damping only halves it. The preregistered settle criterion (peak-to-peak COM envelope over the last 0.05 s) measures oscillation, not drift, so it passed (2.15e-7 L) while the body was still creeping. Mesh 1 and 2 do not show it (12-cycle m2: 6.2e-8 L).",
 "what_is_wrong_with_the_protocol": "the settle criterion missed a drift mode, and dtScale 0.5 is not small enough for passive rest at mesh 3. Both are runner/setup defects, as the falsifier anticipates.",
 "consequence_for_E2_E3": "the same 0.3 s settle at dt0.5 was used for the mesh-3 endpoint runs, so each carries a passive artifact of at most about 7.2e-6 L (the 12-cycle value). Endpoints 2 and 3 are read with the frozen rules unchanged AND with that bound added to every tolerance (stricter, never looser); a verdict is reported as a claim only if it holds under both.",
 "not_done": "the endpoint series was not rerun with a 1 s settle; that would be the clean fix and is listed as next work."
}